  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "THE TRUCK IS THE PROJECTILE\nDrive onto the outlined spring pad at your
    end. Hold your assigned ACTION to charge; steer left/right to aim. Release ACTION
    to commit the visible spring launch. Speed and aim come from your chosen power
    and direction, never automatic homing. After launch, small finite directional
    nudges share one correction budget. Release fore/aft once to arm range correction.
    First table/cup contact ends aftertouch; you cannot drive around the table.\n\nHOUSE
    RULES \xB7 1v1 OR 2v2\nEach side starts with ten hollow red cups. Teams alternate
    one shot whether it hits or misses; teammates alternate their own team's shots.
    A legal shot enters an opposing live cup downward through the open top, then
    penetrates the interior. Rim-in and table-bounce shots each remove ONE cup. Rim
    brushes, exterior/side/bottom entry and flying over cups score nothing. Cup gaps
    remain; no swatting or drinking mechanics.\n\nREBUTTAL\nClearing the final cup
    gives the other side rebuttal. They keep shooting while hitting; their first
    miss loses. Clearing all remaining cups forces three-cup overtime. No counter-rebuttal.
    Overtime alternates the opening team and uses the same rebuttal rule; repeated
    overtime is allowed.\n\nSOLO PRACTICE has unlimited attempts and reracks only
    after clearing all ten. Sources may be shared between turns or assigned separately;
    inactive participants cannot interfere. Pause/reconnect preserves charge, flight
    and cups. Release then freshly hold after a modal confirmation; it cannot accidentally
    fire a charged shot. Recorded replay offers three angles, slow/fast, rewind and
    skip. Offline only."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -7304394381272760782, guid: 8e8f97682e668e94cb30d2e6b8e13d84,
